window.MED_BANK=[{"id":"med-001","concept":"BLS","stem":"A patient becomes unresponsive and is not breathing normally. What is the most appropriate next action?<span class=\"zh\">患者突然无反应且没有正常呼吸。下一步最恰当的行动是什么？</span>","choices":["Place the patient in the recovery position<span class=\"zh\">将患者置于恢复体位</span>","Call 911, obtain the AED and begin CPR<span class=\"zh\">拨打 911、取得 AED 并开始 CPR</span>","Give oral glucose<span class=\"zh\">给予口服葡萄糖</span>","Wait one minute and reassess<span class=\"zh\">等待一分钟后重新评估</span>"],"answer":1,"why":"Correct. Absent normal breathing requires immediate EMS activation, AED retrieval and high-quality CPR.","zh":"正确。无正常呼吸时应立即启动 EMS、取得 AED 并进行高质量 CPR。","pearl":"Prioritize recognition, positioning, airway, breathing, circulation, emergency medication, and EMS activation in the correct sequence.","rationales":[{"en":"Recovery position is for an unconscious patient who is breathing normally; this patient requires resuscitation.","zh":"恢复体位用于无意识但呼吸正常的患者；本例需要复苏。"},{"en":"Correct. Absent normal breathing requires immediate EMS activation, AED retrieval and high-quality CPR.","zh":"正确。无正常呼吸时应立即启动 EMS、取得 AED 并进行高质量 CPR。"},{"en":"Oral glucose is unsafe in an unresponsive patient and does not treat cardiac arrest.","zh":"无反应患者口服葡萄糖不安全，也不能治疗心搏骤停。"},{"en":"Delaying care reduces the chance of survival; action should begin immediately.","zh":"延迟处理会降低生存率，应立即行动。"}]},{"id":"med-002","concept":"BLS","stem":"Which compression rate is recommended for adult CPR?<span class=\"zh\">成人 CPR 推荐的胸外按压频率是多少？</span>","choices":["60-80/min<span class=\"zh\">每分钟 60-80 次</span>","80-90/min<span class=\"zh\">每分钟 80-90 次</span>","100-120/min<span class=\"zh\">每分钟 100-120 次</span>","140-160/min<span class=\"zh\">每分钟 140-160 次</span>"],"answer":2,"why":"Correct. Adult compressions should be delivered at 100-120 per minute with full recoil.","zh":"正确。成人按压频率应为每分钟 100-120 次，并保证充分回弹。","pearl":"Prioritize recognition, positioning, airway, breathing, circulation, emergency medication, and EMS activation in the correct sequence.","rationales":[{"en":"This rate is too slow to provide adequate circulation.","zh":"该频率过慢，无法提供足够循环。"},{"en":"This remains below the recommended adult range.","zh":"仍低于成人推荐范围。"},{"en":"Correct. Adult compressions should be delivered at 100-120 per minute with full recoil.","zh":"正确。成人按压频率应为每分钟 100-120 次，并保证充分回弹。"},{"en":"This rate is excessive and can reduce compression depth and recoil quality.","zh":"该频率过快，可能降低按压深度与回弹质量。"}]},{"id":"med-003","concept":"BLS","stem":"An unconscious patient is breathing normally and has no suspected spinal injury. Which position is most appropriate?<span class=\"zh\">一名无意识患者呼吸正常，且无脊柱损伤嫌疑。最合适的体位是什么？</span>","choices":["Recovery position<span class=\"zh\">恢复体位</span>","Trendelenburg position<span class=\"zh\">头低脚高位</span>","Upright position<span class=\"zh\">直立位</span>","Prone position<span class=\"zh\">俯卧位</span>"],"answer":0,"why":"Correct. The recovery position helps maintain a patent airway while breathing continues.","zh":"正确。恢复体位可在患者仍有呼吸时帮助维持气道通畅。","pearl":"Prioritize recognition, positioning, airway, breathing, circulation, emergency medication, and EMS activation in the correct sequence.","rationales":[{"en":"Correct. The recovery position helps maintain a patent airway while breathing continues.","zh":"正确。恢复体位可在患者仍有呼吸时帮助维持气道通畅。"},{"en":"This position is not the standard choice for an unconscious breathing patient.","zh":"这不是无意识但有呼吸患者的标准体位。"},{"en":"An unconscious patient cannot safely maintain an upright posture.","zh":"无意识患者无法安全保持直立位。"},{"en":"Prone positioning makes airway observation and access more difficult.","zh":"俯卧位会增加气道观察和处理的困难。"}]},{"id":"med-004","concept":"Cardiovascular","stem":"A patient becomes pale, sweaty and light-headed during instrumentation, then briefly loses consciousness. What should be done first?<span class=\"zh\">洁治过程中患者面色苍白、出汗、头晕，随后短暂失去意识。首先应做什么？</span>","choices":["Sit the patient fully upright<span class=\"zh\">让患者完全坐直</span>","Place supine with legs elevated<span class=\"zh\">让患者仰卧并抬高双腿</span>","Give nitroglycerin<span class=\"zh\">给予硝酸甘油</span>","Give insulin<span class=\"zh\">给予胰岛素</span>"],"answer":1,"why":"Correct. Supine positioning with elevated legs improves venous return and cerebral perfusion.","zh":"正确。仰卧抬腿可增加静脉回流并改善脑灌注。","pearl":"Prioritize recognition, positioning, airway, breathing, circulation, emergency medication, and EMS activation in the correct sequence.","rationales":[{"en":"Upright positioning can worsen cerebral hypoperfusion in syncope.","zh":"直立位可能加重晕厥时的脑灌注不足。"},{"en":"Correct. Supine positioning with elevated legs improves venous return and cerebral perfusion.","zh":"正确。仰卧抬腿可增加静脉回流并改善脑灌注。"},{"en":"Nitroglycerin lowers blood pressure and can worsen syncope.","zh":"硝酸甘油会降低血压，可能加重晕厥。"},{"en":"Insulin is unrelated and could cause dangerous hypoglycemia.","zh":"胰岛素与该情况无关，并可能导致危险的低血糖。"}]},{"id":"med-005","concept":"Cardiovascular","stem":"A patient with prescribed nitroglycerin develops their usual exertional chest pressure. What is the best initial management?<span class=\"zh\">一名有硝酸甘油处方的患者出现与以往相同的劳力性胸部压迫感。最佳初始处理是什么？</span>","choices":["Continue treatment and observe<span class=\"zh\">继续治疗并观察</span>","Stop treatment, position comfortably and assist with nitroglycerin<span class=\"zh\">停止治疗、调整舒适体位并协助使用硝酸甘油</span>","Place supine with legs elevated and give glucose<span class=\"zh\">仰卧抬腿并给予葡萄糖</span>","Ask the patient to walk around<span class=\"zh\">让患者走动</span>"],"answer":1,"why":"Correct. Stop care, reduce cardiac workload, assist with prescribed nitroglycerin and monitor closely.","zh":"正确。停止治疗、降低心脏负荷、协助使用处方硝酸甘油并密切监测。","pearl":"Prioritize recognition, positioning, airway, breathing, circulation, emergency medication, and EMS activation in the correct sequence.","rationales":[{"en":"Continuing care increases cardiac demand and ignores a potentially serious symptom.","zh":"继续治疗会增加心脏负荷，并忽视潜在严重症状。"},{"en":"Correct. Stop care, reduce cardiac workload, assist with prescribed nitroglycerin and monitor closely.","zh":"正确。停止治疗、降低心脏负荷、协助使用处方硝酸甘油并密切监测。"},{"en":"This is not typical syncope or hypoglycemia management.","zh":"这不符合典型晕厥或低血糖处理。"},{"en":"Walking increases myocardial oxygen demand and may worsen angina.","zh":"走动会增加心肌耗氧，可能加重心绞痛。"}]},{"id":"med-006","concept":"Cardiovascular","stem":"Chest pain persists despite rest and prescribed nitroglycerin and is accompanied by nausea and sweating. What is the priority?<span class=\"zh\">胸痛在休息及使用处方硝酸甘油后仍持续，并伴恶心和出汗。首要处理是什么？</span>","choices":["Resume care slowly<span class=\"zh\">缓慢恢复治疗</span>","Call 911 and prepare for CPR/AED<span class=\"zh\">拨打 911 并准备 CPR/AED</span>","Give a sugary drink<span class=\"zh\">给予含糖饮料</span>","Send the patient home to rest<span class=\"zh\">让患者回家休息</span>"],"answer":1,"why":"Correct. Ongoing chest pain with autonomic symptoms requires immediate EMS activation and readiness for arrest.","zh":"正确。持续胸痛伴自主神经症状需立即启动 EMS，并准备处理心搏骤停。","pearl":"Prioritize recognition, positioning, airway, breathing, circulation, emergency medication, and EMS activation in the correct sequence.","rationales":[{"en":"Persistent pain may indicate myocardial infarction; care must not resume.","zh":"持续胸痛可能提示心肌梗死，不应恢复治疗。"},{"en":"Correct. Ongoing chest pain with autonomic symptoms requires immediate EMS activation and readiness for arrest.","zh":"正确。持续胸痛伴自主神经症状需立即启动 EMS，并准备处理心搏骤停。"},{"en":"Glucose does not treat acute coronary syndrome.","zh":"葡萄糖不能治疗急性冠脉综合征。"},{"en":"Sending the patient home delays definitive care and is unsafe.","zh":"让患者回家会延误确定性治疗，属不安全做法。"}]},{"id":"med-007","concept":"Cardiovascular","stem":"Which symptom makes a very high blood pressure reading most concerning?<span class=\"zh\">下列哪种症状会使极高血压读数最令人担忧？</span>","choices":["Mild thirst<span class=\"zh\">轻度口渴</span>","Chest pain and new neurologic deficit<span class=\"zh\">胸痛和新发神经功能缺损</span>","Chronic dry mouth<span class=\"zh\">慢性口干</span>","Localized gingival bleeding<span class=\"zh\">局部牙龈出血</span>"],"answer":1,"why":"Correct. Severe hypertension with chest pain or neurologic change suggests acute target-organ injury.","zh":"正确。严重高血压伴胸痛或神经改变提示急性靶器官损伤。","pearl":"Prioritize recognition, positioning, airway, breathing, circulation, emergency medication, and EMS activation in the correct sequence.","rationales":[{"en":"Mild thirst is nonspecific and does not define hypertensive emergency.","zh":"轻度口渴缺乏特异性，并不定义高血压急症。"},{"en":"Correct. Severe hypertension with chest pain or neurologic change suggests acute target-organ injury.","zh":"正确。严重高血压伴胸痛或神经改变提示急性靶器官损伤。"},{"en":"Dry mouth is not a sign of acute hypertensive end-organ damage.","zh":"口干并非急性高血压靶器官损伤的表现。"},{"en":"Localized gingival bleeding does not indicate hypertensive crisis.","zh":"局部牙龈出血不提示高血压危象。"}]},{"id":"med-008","concept":"Respiratory","stem":"A patient with asthma develops wheezing and difficulty exhaling. Which action is best?<span class=\"zh\">哮喘患者出现喘鸣和呼气困难。最佳处理是什么？</span>","choices":["Lay the patient flat<span class=\"zh\">让患者平躺</span>","Assist with the patient's short-acting bronchodilator and sit upright<span class=\"zh\">协助使用短效支气管扩张剂并让患者坐直</span>","Coach rapid breathing<span class=\"zh\">指导快速呼吸</span>","Give oral aspirin<span class=\"zh\">给予口服阿司匹林</span>"],"answer":1,"why":"Correct. Upright positioning and a rescue bronchodilator address bronchospasm directly.","zh":"正确。坐直并使用急救支气管扩张剂可直接处理支气管痉挛。","pearl":"Prioritize recognition, positioning, airway, breathing, circulation, emergency medication, and EMS activation in the correct sequence.","rationales":[{"en":"Flat positioning can worsen breathing discomfort.","zh":"平躺可能加重呼吸不适。"},{"en":"Correct. Upright positioning and a rescue bronchodilator address bronchospasm directly.","zh":"正确。坐直并使用急救支气管扩张剂可直接处理支气管痉挛。"},{"en":"Rapid breathing increases distress and does not relieve bronchospasm.","zh":"快速呼吸会增加痛苦，不能缓解支气管痉挛。"},{"en":"Aspirin does not treat asthma and may trigger symptoms in susceptible patients.","zh":"阿司匹林不能治疗哮喘，且可能诱发敏感患者症状。"}]},{"id":"med-009","concept":"Respiratory","stem":"A visibly anxious patient is breathing rapidly, reports tingling around the mouth and has normal oxygenation. What is the best management?<span class=\"zh\">一名明显焦虑的患者呼吸急促，口周麻刺感，血氧正常。最佳处理是什么？</span>","choices":["Have the patient breathe into a paper bag<span class=\"zh\">让患者对纸袋呼吸</span>","Reassure and coach slow controlled breathing<span class=\"zh\">安抚并指导缓慢、有控制的呼吸</span>","Administer epinephrine immediately<span class=\"zh\">立即给予肾上腺素</span>","Place the patient prone<span class=\"zh\">让患者俯卧</span>"],"answer":1,"why":"Correct. Calm coaching helps reduce respiratory rate and restore carbon dioxide balance.","zh":"正确。平静指导可降低呼吸频率并恢复二氧化碳平衡。","pearl":"Prioritize recognition, positioning, airway, breathing, circulation, emergency medication, and EMS activation in the correct sequence.","rationales":[{"en":"Paper-bag rebreathing is unsafe because another cause of hypoxia may be missed.","zh":"纸袋再呼吸不安全，因为可能漏诊其他缺氧原因。"},{"en":"Correct. Calm coaching helps reduce respiratory rate and restore carbon dioxide balance.","zh":"正确。平静指导可降低呼吸频率并恢复二氧化碳平衡。"},{"en":"Epinephrine is for anaphylaxis, not uncomplicated hyperventilation.","zh":"肾上腺素用于过敏性休克，不用于单纯过度通气。"},{"en":"Prone positioning does not address the cause and impairs observation.","zh":"俯卧位不能处理病因，也不利于观察。"}]},{"id":"med-010","concept":"Respiratory","stem":"A conscious adult cannot speak, cough or breathe after aspirating an object. What is the priority action?<span class=\"zh\">一名清醒成人吸入异物后不能说话、咳嗽或呼吸。首要行动是什么？</span>","choices":["Encourage drinking water<span class=\"zh\">鼓励喝水</span>","Provide abdominal thrusts and activate EMS<span class=\"zh\">实施腹部冲击并启动 EMS</span>","Perform a blind finger sweep<span class=\"zh\">进行盲目手指清扫</span>","Ask the patient to lie down and wait<span class=\"zh\">让患者躺下等待</span>"],"answer":1,"why":"Correct. Complete airway obstruction requires immediate thrusts and emergency activation.","zh":"正确。完全气道阻塞需要立即冲击法并启动急救。","pearl":"Prioritize recognition, positioning, airway, breathing, circulation, emergency medication, and EMS activation in the correct sequence.","rationales":[{"en":"Water can worsen aspiration and the patient cannot safely swallow.","zh":"喝水可能加重误吸，患者也无法安全吞咽。"},{"en":"Correct. Complete airway obstruction requires immediate thrusts and emergency activation.","zh":"正确。完全气道阻塞需要立即冲击法并启动急救。"},{"en":"Blind sweeps can push the object deeper or injure tissues.","zh":"盲目清扫可能把异物推得更深或造成组织损伤。"},{"en":"Waiting allows rapid hypoxia and cardiac arrest to develop.","zh":"等待会导致快速缺氧并可能发生心搏骤停。"}]},{"id":"med-011","concept":"Neurologic","stem":"During a generalized seizure in the dental chair, which action is most appropriate?<span class=\"zh\">患者在牙椅上发生全身性癫痫发作时，哪项处理最恰当？</span>","choices":["Place a mouth prop between the teeth<span class=\"zh\">在牙齿之间放置开口器</span>","Restrain the arms and legs<span class=\"zh\">约束四肢</span>","Remove instruments and protect the patient from injury<span class=\"zh\">移除器械并保护患者免受伤害</span>","Give water immediately<span class=\"zh\">立即给水</span>"],"answer":2,"why":"Correct. Clear the area, lower the chair and prevent injury without restraining the patient.","zh":"正确。清理周围、降低牙椅并防止受伤，但不要约束患者。","pearl":"Prioritize recognition, positioning, airway, breathing, circulation, emergency medication, and EMS activation in the correct sequence.","rationales":[{"en":"Nothing should be placed in the mouth during an active seizure.","zh":"癫痫发作期间不应向口中放入任何物品。"},{"en":"Forceful restraint can cause musculoskeletal injury.","zh":"强行约束可能造成肌肉骨骼损伤。"},{"en":"Correct. Clear the area, lower the chair and prevent injury without restraining the patient.","zh":"正确。清理周围、降低牙椅并防止受伤，但不要约束患者。"},{"en":"Oral fluids create an aspiration risk during and immediately after a seizure.","zh":"发作期间及刚结束时口服液体会增加误吸风险。"}]},{"id":"med-012","concept":"Neurologic","stem":"A patient suddenly develops facial droop, unilateral arm weakness and slurred speech. What should the clinician do?<span class=\"zh\">患者突然出现面部下垂、单侧手臂无力和言语含糊。临床人员应怎么做？</span>","choices":["Give oral glucose and reassess in 30 minutes<span class=\"zh\">给予口服葡萄糖，30 分钟后复查</span>","Call 911 immediately and record symptom onset time<span class=\"zh\">立即拨打 911 并记录症状开始时间</span>","Complete the procedure quickly<span class=\"zh\">快速完成治疗</span>","Place a tablet under the tongue<span class=\"zh\">舌下含服药片</span>"],"answer":1,"why":"Correct. Time-sensitive stroke treatment depends on rapid activation and accurate onset time.","zh":"正确。中风治疗具有时间依赖性，需要快速启动急救并准确记录发病时间。","pearl":"Prioritize recognition, positioning, airway, breathing, circulation, emergency medication, and EMS activation in the correct sequence.","rationales":[{"en":"Hypoglycemia can mimic stroke, but focal FAST findings require urgent EMS evaluation.","zh":"低血糖可类似中风，但局灶性 FAST 表现需要紧急 EMS 评估。"},{"en":"Correct. Time-sensitive stroke treatment depends on rapid activation and accurate onset time.","zh":"正确。中风治疗具有时间依赖性，需要快速启动急救并准确记录发病时间。"},{"en":"Continuing treatment delays emergency care.","zh":"继续治疗会延误急救。"},{"en":"No unspecified sublingual tablet is appropriate for suspected stroke.","zh":"疑似中风时没有适合的未明确舌下药物。"}]},{"id":"med-013","concept":"Allergy","stem":"A patient develops localized itching and a few hives without breathing difficulty or hypotension. Which statement is most accurate?<span class=\"zh\">患者出现局部瘙痒和少量荨麻疹，但无呼吸困难或低血压。哪项说法最准确？</span>","choices":["This is definitely cardiac arrest<span class=\"zh\">这肯定是心搏骤停</span>","Monitor closely; an antihistamine may help, but watch for progression<span class=\"zh\">密切监测；抗组胺药可能有帮助，但需观察是否进展</span>","Give insulin immediately<span class=\"zh\">立即给予胰岛素</span>","Continue treatment because symptoms are minor<span class=\"zh\">因症状轻微而继续治疗</span>"],"answer":1,"why":"Correct. Mild allergy may be treated supportively, but progression toward anaphylaxis must be watched carefully.","zh":"正确。轻度过敏可支持治疗，但必须密切观察是否进展为过敏性休克。","pearl":"Prioritize recognition, positioning, airway, breathing, circulation, emergency medication, and EMS activation in the correct sequence.","rationales":[{"en":"The patient is conscious with isolated skin findings, not cardiac arrest.","zh":"患者清醒且仅有皮肤表现，不是心搏骤停。"},{"en":"Correct. Mild allergy may be treated supportively, but progression toward anaphylaxis must be watched carefully.","zh":"正确。轻度过敏可支持治疗，但必须密切观察是否进展为过敏性休克。"},{"en":"Insulin has no role in allergy management.","zh":"胰岛素在过敏处理中无作用。"},{"en":"Exposure should stop and the patient should be assessed rather than treatment continuing.","zh":"应停止接触并评估患者，而不是继续治疗。"}]},{"id":"med-014","concept":"Allergy","stem":"A patient develops wheezing, facial swelling and hypotension after latex exposure. What is the first-line medication?<span class=\"zh\">患者接触乳胶后出现喘鸣、面部肿胀和低血压。首选药物是什么？</span>","choices":["Oral diphenhydramine only<span class=\"zh\">仅口服苯海拉明</span>","Intramuscular epinephrine<span class=\"zh\">肌内注射肾上腺素</span>","Nitroglycerin<span class=\"zh\">硝酸甘油</span>","Aspirin<span class=\"zh\">阿司匹林</span>"],"answer":1,"why":"Correct. IM epinephrine in the anterolateral thigh is first-line treatment for anaphylaxis.","zh":"正确。大腿前外侧肌内注射肾上腺素是过敏性休克的一线治疗。","pearl":"Prioritize recognition, positioning, airway, breathing, circulation, emergency medication, and EMS activation in the correct sequence.","rationales":[{"en":"Antihistamine is too slow and does not reverse airway obstruction or shock.","zh":"抗组胺药起效过慢，不能逆转气道阻塞或休克。"},{"en":"Correct. IM epinephrine in the anterolateral thigh is first-line treatment for anaphylaxis.","zh":"正确。大腿前外侧肌内注射肾上腺素是过敏性休克的一线治疗。"},{"en":"Nitroglycerin can worsen hypotension and does not treat anaphylaxis.","zh":"硝酸甘油会加重低血压，也不能治疗过敏性休克。"},{"en":"Aspirin has no role and may worsen reactions in some patients.","zh":"阿司匹林无治疗作用，且可能加重部分患者的反应。"}]},{"id":"med-015","concept":"Allergy","stem":"After giving epinephrine for anaphylaxis, what should happen next?<span class=\"zh\">给予肾上腺素治疗过敏性休克后，下一步应做什么？</span>","choices":["Dismiss the patient once hives fade<span class=\"zh\">荨麻疹减轻后让患者离开</span>","Call 911, provide oxygen, monitor and prepare to repeat epinephrine if needed<span class=\"zh\">拨打 911、给氧、监测，并准备必要时重复肾上腺素</span>","Continue dental treatment<span class=\"zh\">继续牙科治疗</span>","Give food and drink<span class=\"zh\">给予食物和饮料</span>"],"answer":1,"why":"Correct. Epinephrine is followed by EMS activation, supportive care and reassessment for repeat dosing.","zh":"正确。肾上腺素后应启动 EMS、进行支持治疗，并评估是否需重复给药。","pearl":"Prioritize recognition, positioning, airway, breathing, circulation, emergency medication, and EMS activation in the correct sequence.","rationales":[{"en":"Anaphylaxis can recur or worsen; emergency observation is required.","zh":"过敏性休克可能复发或恶化，需要急救观察。"},{"en":"Correct. Epinephrine is followed by EMS activation, supportive care and reassessment for repeat dosing.","zh":"正确。肾上腺素后应启动 EMS、进行支持治疗，并评估是否需重复给药。"},{"en":"Treatment must stop because the condition is life-threatening.","zh":"由于病情危及生命，必须停止牙科治疗。"},{"en":"Oral intake is unsafe with airway swelling or altered consciousness.","zh":"存在气道肿胀或意识改变时，口服摄入不安全。"}]},{"id":"med-016","concept":"Diabetes","stem":"An alert patient with diabetes becomes shaky, sweaty and confused. What is the best immediate treatment?<span class=\"zh\">一名清醒的糖尿病患者出现颤抖、出汗和意识混乱。最佳立即处理是什么？</span>","choices":["Fast-acting oral glucose<span class=\"zh\">速效口服葡萄糖</span>","Additional insulin<span class=\"zh\">追加胰岛素</span>","Nitroglycerin<span class=\"zh\">硝酸甘油</span>","Restrict all carbohydrates<span class=\"zh\">限制所有碳水化合物</span>"],"answer":0,"why":"Correct. The symptoms are classic for hypoglycemia, and an alert patient can receive oral glucose.","zh":"正确。这些是典型低血糖表现，清醒患者可给予口服葡萄糖。","pearl":"Prioritize recognition, positioning, airway, breathing, circulation, emergency medication, and EMS activation in the correct sequence.","rationales":[{"en":"Correct. The symptoms are classic for hypoglycemia, and an alert patient can receive oral glucose.","zh":"正确。这些是典型低血糖表现，清醒患者可给予口服葡萄糖。"},{"en":"Insulin would lower glucose further and may cause coma.","zh":"胰岛素会进一步降低血糖，可能导致昏迷。"},{"en":"Nitroglycerin treats angina, not hypoglycemia.","zh":"硝酸甘油治疗心绞痛，不治疗低血糖。"},{"en":"Carbohydrate restriction worsens the immediate glucose deficit.","zh":"限制碳水会加重当前的葡萄糖不足。"}]},{"id":"med-017","concept":"Diabetes","stem":"A hypoglycemic patient is unconscious and cannot swallow safely. What is the best action?<span class=\"zh\">低血糖患者无意识，无法安全吞咽。最佳行动是什么？</span>","choices":["Place glucose gel deep in the mouth<span class=\"zh\">将葡萄糖凝胶放入口腔深处</span>","Call EMS and administer glucagon according to protocol<span class=\"zh\">启动 EMS，并按方案给予胰高血糖素</span>","Give a glass of juice<span class=\"zh\">给予一杯果汁</span>","Wait for spontaneous recovery<span class=\"zh\">等待自行恢复</span>"],"answer":1,"why":"Correct. Severe hypoglycemia requires emergency activation and non-oral glucose rescue such as glucagon when available.","zh":"正确。重度低血糖需启动急救，并在可用时采用胰高血糖素等非口服救援。","pearl":"Prioritize recognition, positioning, airway, breathing, circulation, emergency medication, and EMS activation in the correct sequence.","rationales":[{"en":"Placing glucose in the mouth of an unconscious patient risks aspiration.","zh":"无意识患者口中放入葡萄糖会增加误吸风险。"},{"en":"Correct. Severe hypoglycemia requires emergency activation and non-oral glucose rescue such as glucagon when available.","zh":"正确。重度低血糖需启动急救，并在可用时采用胰高血糖素等非口服救援。"},{"en":"Juice is unsafe because swallowing is impaired.","zh":"因吞咽受损，果汁不安全。"},{"en":"Untreated hypoglycemia can cause brain injury or death.","zh":"未处理的低血糖可导致脑损伤或死亡。"}]},{"id":"med-018","concept":"Diabetes","stem":"Which finding is more consistent with hyperglycemia than hypoglycemia?<span class=\"zh\">下列哪项更符合高血糖而非低血糖？</span>","choices":["Rapid onset sweating and tremor<span class=\"zh\">快速出现出汗和颤抖</span>","Gradual thirst, frequent urination and dry skin<span class=\"zh\">逐渐出现口渴、尿频和皮肤干燥</span>","Immediate improvement after oral glucose<span class=\"zh\">口服葡萄糖后立即改善</span>","Sudden hunger and irritability<span class=\"zh\">突然饥饿和烦躁</span>"],"answer":1,"why":"Correct. Hyperglycemia usually develops gradually with dehydration-related symptoms.","zh":"正确。高血糖通常逐渐发展，并出现脱水相关症状。","pearl":"Prioritize recognition, positioning, airway, breathing, circulation, emergency medication, and EMS activation in the correct sequence.","rationales":[{"en":"These adrenergic symptoms are typical of hypoglycemia.","zh":"这些肾上腺素能症状典型见于低血糖。"},{"en":"Correct. Hyperglycemia usually develops gradually with dehydration-related symptoms.","zh":"正确。高血糖通常逐渐发展，并出现脱水相关症状。"},{"en":"Improvement after glucose supports hypoglycemia, not hyperglycemia.","zh":"葡萄糖后改善支持低血糖，而非高血糖。"},{"en":"Sudden hunger and irritability are common in hypoglycemia.","zh":"突然饥饿和烦躁常见于低血糖。"}]},{"id":"med-019","concept":"Toxicity","stem":"Immediately after a rapid local anesthetic injection, a patient reports metallic taste, tinnitus and circumoral numbness. What should be suspected?<span class=\"zh\">快速注射局麻药后，患者立即出现金属味、耳鸣和口周麻木。应怀疑什么？</span>","choices":["Local anesthetic systemic toxicity<span class=\"zh\">局麻药全身毒性</span>","Simple syncope only<span class=\"zh\">单纯晕厥</span>","Hyperglycemia<span class=\"zh\">高血糖</span>","Dry socket<span class=\"zh\">干槽症</span>"],"answer":0,"why":"Correct. Early neurologic symptoms after injection are classic warning signs of systemic local anesthetic toxicity.","zh":"正确。注射后出现早期神经症状是局麻药全身毒性的典型警示。","pearl":"Prioritize recognition, positioning, airway, breathing, circulation, emergency medication, and EMS activation in the correct sequence.","rationales":[{"en":"Correct. Early neurologic symptoms after injection are classic warning signs of systemic local anesthetic toxicity.","zh":"正确。注射后出现早期神经症状是局麻药全身毒性的典型警示。"},{"en":"Syncope more often presents with pallor, sweating and transient loss of consciousness rather than metallic taste and tinnitus.","zh":"晕厥更常见苍白、出汗和短暂意识丧失，而非金属味和耳鸣。"},{"en":"Hyperglycemia does not begin immediately after local anesthetic injection with these neurologic symptoms.","zh":"高血糖不会在局麻注射后立即以这些神经症状出现。"},{"en":"Dry socket occurs days after extraction and causes localized pain.","zh":"干槽症发生于拔牙后数日，并表现为局部疼痛。"}]},{"id":"med-020","concept":"Toxicity","stem":"What is the first action when significant local anesthetic toxicity is suspected?<span class=\"zh\">怀疑明显局麻药毒性时，第一步是什么？</span>","choices":["Continue injecting more slowly<span class=\"zh\">继续注射但减慢速度</span>","Stop injection and call for help<span class=\"zh\">停止注射并呼叫帮助</span>","Give the patient food<span class=\"zh\">给患者食物</span>","Discharge the patient<span class=\"zh\">让患者离开</span>"],"answer":1,"why":"Correct. Stop the source immediately, summon help and support airway, breathing and circulation.","zh":"正确。立即停止药物来源、呼叫帮助，并支持气道、呼吸和循环。","pearl":"Prioritize recognition, positioning, airway, breathing, circulation, emergency medication, and EMS activation in the correct sequence.","rationales":[{"en":"Any further drug increases the toxic dose.","zh":"继续给药会增加毒性剂量。"},{"en":"Correct. Stop the source immediately, summon help and support airway, breathing and circulation.","zh":"正确。立即停止药物来源、呼叫帮助，并支持气道、呼吸和循环。"},{"en":"Food does not reverse systemic toxicity and may create aspiration risk.","zh":"食物不能逆转全身毒性，还可能增加误吸风险。"},{"en":"Potential toxicity requires monitoring and possibly EMS, not discharge.","zh":"潜在毒性需要监测并可能启动 EMS，不能直接离开。"}]},{"id":"med-021","concept":"Dental complications","stem":"A permanent tooth is completely avulsed. Which handling method is correct?<span class=\"zh\">恒牙完全脱位。正确的处理方法是什么？</span>","choices":["Hold the tooth by the root and scrub it<span class=\"zh\">抓住牙根并刷洗</span>","Hold the tooth by the crown and avoid touching the root<span class=\"zh\">握住牙冠并避免触碰牙根</span>","Let the tooth dry on gauze<span class=\"zh\">将牙齿放在纱布上晾干</span>","Discard the tooth<span class=\"zh\">丢弃牙齿</span>"],"answer":1,"why":"Correct. Crown-only handling preserves fragile root surface cells.","zh":"正确。只握牙冠可保护脆弱的牙根表面细胞。","pearl":"Prioritize recognition, positioning, airway, breathing, circulation, emergency medication, and EMS activation in the correct sequence.","rationales":[{"en":"Root handling and scrubbing damage periodontal ligament cells needed for replantation.","zh":"触碰和刷洗牙根会损伤再植所需的牙周膜细胞。"},{"en":"Correct. Crown-only handling preserves fragile root surface cells.","zh":"正确。只握牙冠可保护脆弱的牙根表面细胞。"},{"en":"Dry storage rapidly reduces periodontal ligament cell survival.","zh":"干燥保存会迅速降低牙周膜细胞存活率。"},{"en":"A permanent avulsed tooth may be salvageable and should not be discarded.","zh":"脱位恒牙可能可以挽救，不应丢弃。"}]},{"id":"med-022","concept":"Dental complications","stem":"A patient has persistent bleeding after extraction. What is the best first measure?<span class=\"zh\">患者拔牙后持续出血。最佳首要措施是什么？</span>","choices":["Firm direct pressure with gauze<span class=\"zh\">用纱布持续直接加压</span>","Frequent vigorous rinsing<span class=\"zh\">频繁用力漱口</span>","Remove the clot repeatedly<span class=\"zh\">反复去除血凝块</span>","Apply heat to the face<span class=\"zh\">面部热敷</span>"],"answer":0,"why":"Correct. Continuous direct pressure supports clot formation and is the initial local measure.","zh":"正确。持续直接加压有助于血凝块形成，是首选局部措施。","pearl":"Prioritize recognition, positioning, airway, breathing, circulation, emergency medication, and EMS activation in the correct sequence.","rationales":[{"en":"Correct. Continuous direct pressure supports clot formation and is the initial local measure.","zh":"正确。持续直接加压有助于血凝块形成，是首选局部措施。"},{"en":"Vigorous rinsing disrupts the clot and can prolong bleeding.","zh":"用力漱口会破坏血凝块并延长出血。"},{"en":"Removing the clot prevents stable hemostasis.","zh":"去除血凝块会妨碍稳定止血。"},{"en":"Heat causes vasodilation and may worsen bleeding.","zh":"热敷会导致血管扩张，可能加重出血。"}]},{"id":"med-023","concept":"Dental complications","stem":"A patient develops severe throbbing pain three days after extraction, with an empty-appearing socket and foul taste. What is most likely?<span class=\"zh\">患者拔牙后三天出现剧烈搏动性疼痛，牙槽窝看似空虚并有异味。最可能是什么？</span>","choices":["Dry socket<span class=\"zh\">干槽症</span>","Anaphylaxis<span class=\"zh\">过敏性休克</span>","Hypoglycemia<span class=\"zh\">低血糖</span>","Syncope<span class=\"zh\">晕厥</span>"],"answer":0,"why":"Correct. Delayed severe pain with loss of the clot is characteristic of alveolar osteitis (dry socket).","zh":"正确。拔牙后延迟出现剧痛并伴血凝块丢失，符合牙槽骨炎（干槽症）。","pearl":"Prioritize recognition, positioning, airway, breathing, circulation, emergency medication, and EMS activation in the correct sequence.","rationales":[{"en":"Correct. Delayed severe pain with loss of the clot is characteristic of alveolar osteitis (dry socket).","zh":"正确。拔牙后延迟出现剧痛并伴血凝块丢失，符合牙槽骨炎（干槽症）。"},{"en":"Anaphylaxis is an acute systemic allergic reaction, not a delayed localized socket problem.","zh":"过敏性休克是急性全身过敏反应，不是延迟的局部牙槽窝问题。"},{"en":"Hypoglycemia causes systemic neuroglycopenic and adrenergic symptoms, not an empty socket.","zh":"低血糖引起全身神经低糖和肾上腺素能症状，不会导致牙槽窝空虚。"},{"en":"Syncope is transient loss of consciousness, unrelated to delayed extraction pain.","zh":"晕厥是短暂意识丧失，与拔牙后延迟疼痛无关。"}]},{"id":"med-024","concept":"Dental complications","stem":"After a posterior superior alveolar injection, rapid cheek swelling develops. What is the most likely complication?<span class=\"zh\">上牙槽后神经阻滞注射后，面颊迅速肿胀。最可能的并发症是什么？</span>","choices":["Hematoma<span class=\"zh\">血肿</span>","Dry socket<span class=\"zh\">干槽症</span>","Stroke<span class=\"zh\">中风</span>","Hyperventilation<span class=\"zh\">过度通气</span>"],"answer":0,"why":"Correct. Vessel injury during injection can cause rapid soft-tissue bleeding and hematoma formation.","zh":"正确。注射时损伤血管可导致软组织快速出血并形成血肿。","pearl":"Prioritize recognition, positioning, airway, breathing, circulation, emergency medication, and EMS activation in the correct sequence.","rationales":[{"en":"Correct. Vessel injury during injection can cause rapid soft-tissue bleeding and hematoma formation.","zh":"正确。注射时损伤血管可导致软组织快速出血并形成血肿。"},{"en":"Dry socket follows extraction and does not cause immediate cheek swelling after injection.","zh":"干槽症发生于拔牙后，不会在注射后立即导致面颊肿胀。"},{"en":"Stroke causes focal neurologic deficits, not isolated injection-site swelling.","zh":"中风引起局灶性神经缺损，而非单纯注射部位肿胀。"},{"en":"Hyperventilation causes rapid breathing and tingling, not localized swelling.","zh":"过度通气引起呼吸加快和麻刺感，不会导致局部肿胀。"}]},{"id":"med-025","concept":"Priorities","stem":"Which emergency medication should be given first for anaphylaxis?<span class=\"zh\">过敏性休克时应首先给予哪种急救药物？</span>","choices":["Epinephrine<span class=\"zh\">肾上腺素</span>","Diphenhydramine<span class=\"zh\">苯海拉明</span>","Albuterol only<span class=\"zh\">仅沙丁胺醇</span>","Aspirin<span class=\"zh\">阿司匹林</span>"],"answer":0,"why":"Correct. Epinephrine rapidly treats airway edema, bronchospasm and shock.","zh":"正确。肾上腺素可快速处理气道水肿、支气管痉挛和休克。","pearl":"Prioritize recognition, positioning, airway, breathing, circulation, emergency medication, and EMS activation in the correct sequence.","rationales":[{"en":"Correct. Epinephrine rapidly treats airway edema, bronchospasm and shock.","zh":"正确。肾上腺素可快速处理气道水肿、支气管痉挛和休克。"},{"en":"Antihistamines are adjuncts and do not act fast enough for life-threatening anaphylaxis.","zh":"抗组胺药仅为辅助，起效不足以处理危及生命的过敏性休克。"},{"en":"Albuterol may help bronchospasm but does not treat vascular collapse or airway edema.","zh":"沙丁胺醇可缓解支气管痉挛，但不能处理血管性休克或气道水肿。"},{"en":"Aspirin has no role in anaphylaxis.","zh":"阿司匹林在过敏性休克中无作用。"}]},{"id":"med-026","concept":"Priorities","stem":"Which patient should NOT receive anything by mouth?<span class=\"zh\">哪位患者不应口服任何东西？</span>","choices":["Alert patient with mild hypoglycemia<span class=\"zh\">清醒且轻度低血糖患者</span>","Unconscious patient after a seizure<span class=\"zh\">癫痫发作后无意识患者</span>","Alert patient with dry mouth<span class=\"zh\">清醒且口干患者</span>","Alert patient with mild anxiety<span class=\"zh\">清醒且轻度焦虑患者</span>"],"answer":1,"why":"Correct. Impaired consciousness makes oral intake unsafe because of aspiration risk.","zh":"正确。意识受损时口服摄入会造成误吸风险。","pearl":"Prioritize recognition, positioning, airway, breathing, circulation, emergency medication, and EMS activation in the correct sequence.","rationales":[{"en":"An alert patient who can swallow may receive oral glucose.","zh":"能安全吞咽的清醒患者可口服葡萄糖。"},{"en":"Correct. Impaired consciousness makes oral intake unsafe because of aspiration risk.","zh":"正确。意识受损时口服摄入会造成误吸风险。"},{"en":"Dry mouth alone does not necessarily prevent safe oral intake.","zh":"单纯口干通常不妨碍安全口服。"},{"en":"Mild anxiety does not automatically make swallowing unsafe.","zh":"轻度焦虑并不意味着吞咽不安全。"}]},{"id":"med-027","concept":"Priorities","stem":"Which action is contraindicated during an active seizure?<span class=\"zh\">癫痫正在发作时，哪项操作属于禁忌？</span>","choices":["Removing nearby instruments<span class=\"zh\">移除附近器械</span>","Protecting the head<span class=\"zh\">保护头部</span>","Placing an object between the teeth<span class=\"zh\">在牙齿之间放置物品</span>","Timing the seizure<span class=\"zh\">记录发作持续时间</span>"],"answer":2,"why":"Correct. Objects in the mouth can damage teeth and tissues and obstruct the airway.","zh":"正确。口中放置物品可能损伤牙齿和组织，并阻塞气道。","pearl":"Prioritize recognition, positioning, airway, breathing, circulation, emergency medication, and EMS activation in the correct sequence.","rationales":[{"en":"Removing hazards reduces injury risk.","zh":"移除危险物可降低受伤风险。"},{"en":"Protecting the head is appropriate supportive care.","zh":"保护头部是适当的支持措施。"},{"en":"Correct. Objects in the mouth can damage teeth and tissues and obstruct the airway.","zh":"正确。口中放置物品可能损伤牙齿和组织，并阻塞气道。"},{"en":"Timing helps determine whether prolonged seizure activity requires urgent escalation.","zh":"计时有助于判断持续发作是否需要紧急升级处理。"}]},{"id":"med-028","concept":"Priorities","stem":"A patient has suspected myocardial infarction and no aspirin allergy, active bleeding or other contraindication. Which adjunct may be appropriate while awaiting EMS?<span class=\"zh\">疑似心肌梗死患者无阿司匹林过敏、活动性出血或其他禁忌。等待 EMS 时可考虑哪种辅助措施？</span>","choices":["Chewable aspirin<span class=\"zh\">嚼服阿司匹林</span>","Additional insulin<span class=\"zh\">追加胰岛素</span>","Oral antihistamine only<span class=\"zh\">仅口服抗组胺药</span>","Paper-bag breathing<span class=\"zh\">纸袋呼吸</span>"],"answer":0,"why":"Correct. Chewed aspirin may reduce platelet aggregation in suspected acute coronary syndrome when not contraindicated.","zh":"正确。无禁忌时，嚼服阿司匹林可在疑似急性冠脉综合征中减少血小板聚集。","pearl":"Prioritize recognition, positioning, airway, breathing, circulation, emergency medication, and EMS activation in the correct sequence.","rationales":[{"en":"Correct. Chewed aspirin may reduce platelet aggregation in suspected acute coronary syndrome when not contraindicated.","zh":"正确。无禁忌时，嚼服阿司匹林可在疑似急性冠脉综合征中减少血小板聚集。"},{"en":"Insulin does not treat myocardial infarction and may cause hypoglycemia.","zh":"胰岛素不能治疗心肌梗死，并可能导致低血糖。"},{"en":"Antihistamine does not treat coronary thrombosis.","zh":"抗组胺药不能治疗冠状动脉血栓。"},{"en":"Paper-bag breathing is unrelated and potentially unsafe.","zh":"纸袋呼吸与此无关且可能不安全。"}]},{"id":"med-029","concept":"Priorities","stem":"Which event requires immediate EMS activation even if symptoms begin to improve?<span class=\"zh\">哪种情况即使症状开始改善也需要立即启动 EMS？</span>","choices":["Brief mild anxiety<span class=\"zh\">短暂轻度焦虑</span>","Anaphylaxis treated with epinephrine<span class=\"zh\">已用肾上腺素治疗的过敏性休克</span>","Localized mild gingival bleeding<span class=\"zh\">局部轻度牙龈出血</span>","Transient dry mouth<span class=\"zh\">短暂口干</span>"],"answer":1,"why":"Correct. Anaphylaxis can recur and requires emergency evaluation after epinephrine.","zh":"正确。过敏性休克可复发，使用肾上腺素后仍需急诊评估。","pearl":"Prioritize recognition, positioning, airway, breathing, circulation, emergency medication, and EMS activation in the correct sequence.","rationales":[{"en":"Mild anxiety usually responds to reassurance and monitoring.","zh":"轻度焦虑通常可通过安抚和监测处理。"},{"en":"Correct. Anaphylaxis can recur and requires emergency evaluation after epinephrine.","zh":"正确。过敏性休克可复发，使用肾上腺素后仍需急诊评估。"},{"en":"Localized mild bleeding is generally managed locally unless persistent or severe.","zh":"局部轻度出血通常可局部处理，除非持续或严重。"},{"en":"Dry mouth alone is not an EMS-level emergency.","zh":"单纯口干不属于 EMS 级别急症。"}]},{"id":"med-030","concept":"Documentation","stem":"After an emergency has resolved, which documentation is most complete?<span class=\"zh\">急症处理结束后，哪项记录最完整？</span>","choices":["Only the final diagnosis<span class=\"zh\">只记录最终诊断</span>","Symptoms, vital signs, timeline, interventions, medication details, response and disposition<span class=\"zh\">症状、生命体征、时间线、干预、药物详情、反应及后续处置</span>","Only the medication name<span class=\"zh\">只记录药名</span>","No documentation if EMS was called<span class=\"zh\">若已呼叫 EMS 则无需记录</span>"],"answer":1,"why":"Correct. A complete contemporaneous record supports continuity, safety and legal accountability.","zh":"正确。完整的即时记录有助于连续照护、安全与法律责任。","pearl":"Prioritize recognition, positioning, airway, breathing, circulation, emergency medication, and EMS activation in the correct sequence.","rationales":[{"en":"A diagnosis alone does not capture what occurred or how the patient responded.","zh":"仅记录诊断不能反映事件经过及患者反应。"},{"en":"Correct. A complete contemporaneous record supports continuity, safety and legal accountability.","zh":"正确。完整的即时记录有助于连续照护、安全与法律责任。"},{"en":"Medication name without dose, route, time and effect is incomplete.","zh":"仅记录药名而无剂量、途径、时间和效果是不完整的。"},{"en":"EMS involvement increases, rather than removes, the need for detailed documentation.","zh":"EMS 介入反而增加详细记录的必要性。"}]},{"id":"med-031","concept":"BLS","stem":"An adult is unresponsive, has no normal breathing, and no definite pulse is felt within 10 seconds. Which compression-to-ventilation ratio should a single rescuer use?<span class=\"zh\">成人无反应、无正常呼吸，且在 10 秒内未明确触及脉搏。单人施救者应使用哪种按压与通气比例？</span>","choices":["15:2<span class=\"zh\">15:2</span>","30:1<span class=\"zh\">30:1</span>","30:2<span class=\"zh\">30:2</span>","5:1<span class=\"zh\">5:1</span>"],"answer":2,"why":"Correct. Adult single-rescuer CPR uses 30 compressions followed by 2 breaths.","zh":"正确。成人单人 CPR 使用 30 次按压后给予 2 次呼吸。","pearl":"In emergencies, recognize the pattern, stop care, position appropriately, support ABCs, give the indicated drug, and activate EMS without delay when needed.","rationales":[{"en":"15:2 is the two-rescuer ratio commonly used for children and infants, not a single adult rescuer.","zh":"15:2 常用于儿童和婴儿的双人施救，不适用于成人单人施救。"},{"en":"30:1 does not provide the recommended ventilation frequency.","zh":"30:1 不能提供推荐的通气频率。"},{"en":"Correct. Adult single-rescuer CPR uses 30 compressions followed by 2 breaths.","zh":"正确。成人单人 CPR 使用 30 次按压后给予 2 次呼吸。"},{"en":"5:1 is an outdated ratio and is not recommended.","zh":"5:1 是过时比例，不再推荐。"}]},{"id":"med-032","concept":"BLS","stem":"During adult CPR, what compression depth is most appropriate?<span class=\"zh\">成人 CPR 时，胸外按压深度最合适的是多少？</span>","choices":["About 1 cm<span class=\"zh\">约 1 厘米</span>","About 2 cm<span class=\"zh\">约 2 厘米</span>","At least 5 cm but not more than 6 cm<span class=\"zh\">至少 5 厘米但不超过 6 厘米</span>","More than 8 cm<span class=\"zh\">超过 8 厘米</span>"],"answer":2,"why":"Correct. Adult compressions should be about 5 to 6 cm deep while allowing full chest recoil.","zh":"正确。成人按压深度约为 5 至 6 厘米，并应让胸廓充分回弹。","pearl":"In emergencies, recognize the pattern, stop care, position appropriately, support ABCs, give the indicated drug, and activate EMS without delay when needed.","rationales":[{"en":"One centimetre is too shallow to generate adequate blood flow.","zh":"1 厘米过浅，无法产生足够血流。"},{"en":"Two centimetres is still too shallow for adult CPR.","zh":"2 厘米对成人 CPR 仍然过浅。"},{"en":"Correct. Adult compressions should be about 5 to 6 cm deep while allowing full chest recoil.","zh":"正确。成人按压深度约为 5 至 6 厘米，并应让胸廓充分回弹。"},{"en":"Excessive depth increases injury risk without improving resuscitation quality.","zh":"过深会增加损伤风险，并不会改善复苏质量。"}]},{"id":"med-033","concept":"BLS","stem":"The AED announces “no shock advised” while the patient remains pulseless. What should the team do next?<span class=\"zh\">AED 提示“不建议电击”，但患者仍无脉搏。团队下一步应做什么？</span>","choices":["Remove the pads and wait<span class=\"zh\">取下电极片并等待</span>","Immediately resume CPR for about 2 minutes<span class=\"zh\">立即恢复 CPR 约 2 分钟</span>","Give oral glucose<span class=\"zh\">给予口服葡萄糖</span>","Place the patient in the recovery position<span class=\"zh\">将患者置于恢复体位</span>"],"answer":1,"why":"Correct. CPR should resume immediately after any AED analysis when no shock is advised.","zh":"正确。AED 分析后若不建议电击，应立即恢复 CPR。","pearl":"In emergencies, recognize the pattern, stop care, position appropriately, support ABCs, give the indicated drug, and activate EMS without delay when needed.","rationales":[{"en":"Removing pads delays reassessment and further AED use.","zh":"取下电极片会延误再次评估和后续 AED 使用。"},{"en":"Correct. CPR should resume immediately after any AED analysis when no shock is advised.","zh":"正确。AED 分析后若不建议电击，应立即恢复 CPR。"},{"en":"Oral glucose is unsafe and irrelevant in cardiac arrest.","zh":"心搏骤停时口服葡萄糖不安全且无关。"},{"en":"Recovery position is only for an unconscious patient who is breathing normally.","zh":"恢复体位仅用于无意识但呼吸正常的患者。"}]},{"id":"med-034","concept":"Cardiovascular","stem":"Before assisting a patient with nitroglycerin for chest pain, which recent medication history is most critical?<span class=\"zh\">协助胸痛患者使用硝酸甘油前，哪项近期用药史最关键？</span>","choices":["A topical fluoride treatment<span class=\"zh\">局部氟化物治疗</span>","A phosphodiesterase-5 inhibitor such as sildenafil<span class=\"zh\">磷酸二酯酶-5 抑制剂，如西地那非</span>","An antihistamine taken yesterday<span class=\"zh\">昨天服用的抗组胺药</span>","A multivitamin<span class=\"zh\">复合维生素</span>"],"answer":1,"why":"Correct. PDE-5 inhibitors combined with nitroglycerin can cause profound, dangerous hypotension.","zh":"正确。PDE-5 抑制剂与硝酸甘油合用可导致严重而危险的低血压。","pearl":"In emergencies, recognize the pattern, stop care, position appropriately, support ABCs, give the indicated drug, and activate EMS without delay when needed.","rationales":[{"en":"Topical fluoride does not create this cardiovascular interaction.","zh":"局部氟化物不会产生这种心血管相互作用。"},{"en":"Correct. PDE-5 inhibitors combined with nitroglycerin can cause profound, dangerous hypotension.","zh":"正确。PDE-5 抑制剂与硝酸甘油合用可导致严重而危险的低血压。"},{"en":"A routine antihistamine is not the key contraindication to nitroglycerin here.","zh":"常规抗组胺药不是此处硝酸甘油的关键禁忌。"},{"en":"A multivitamin does not meaningfully interact with nitroglycerin.","zh":"复合维生素与硝酸甘油无显著相互作用。"}]},{"id":"med-035","concept":"Cardiovascular","stem":"A conscious patient has suspected myocardial infarction and no aspirin allergy, active bleeding, or other contraindication. Which medication may be appropriate while awaiting EMS?<span class=\"zh\">一名清醒患者疑似心肌梗死，且无阿司匹林过敏、活动性出血或其他禁忌。等待 EMS 时可考虑哪种药物？</span>","choices":["Chewable aspirin<span class=\"zh\">可咀嚼阿司匹林</span>","Insulin<span class=\"zh\">胰岛素</span>","Diphenhydramine<span class=\"zh\">苯海拉明</span>","Naloxone<span class=\"zh\">纳洛酮</span>"],"answer":0,"why":"Correct. Chewed aspirin may reduce platelet aggregation in suspected myocardial infarction when not contraindicated.","zh":"正确。在无禁忌时，咀嚼阿司匹林可减少疑似心肌梗死患者的血小板聚集。","pearl":"In emergencies, recognize the pattern, stop care, position appropriately, support ABCs, give the indicated drug, and activate EMS without delay when needed.","rationales":[{"en":"Correct. Chewed aspirin may reduce platelet aggregation in suspected myocardial infarction when not contraindicated.","zh":"正确。在无禁忌时，咀嚼阿司匹林可减少疑似心肌梗死患者的血小板聚集。"},{"en":"Insulin does not treat acute coronary thrombosis and could cause hypoglycemia.","zh":"胰岛素不能治疗急性冠状动脉血栓，并可能导致低血糖。"},{"en":"Diphenhydramine treats allergic symptoms, not myocardial infarction.","zh":"苯海拉明用于过敏症状，不治疗心肌梗死。"},{"en":"Naloxone reverses opioid toxicity, not acute coronary syndrome.","zh":"纳洛酮用于逆转阿片类药物中毒，不治疗急性冠脉综合征。"}]},{"id":"med-036","concept":"Cardiovascular","stem":"A patient with suspected stroke has facial droop and arm weakness. Which positioning is most appropriate while awaiting EMS if the patient is conscious and breathing?<span class=\"zh\">疑似卒中患者出现面部下垂和手臂无力。若患者清醒且有呼吸，等待 EMS 时最合适的体位是什么？</span>","choices":["Force the patient to walk<span class=\"zh\">强迫患者行走</span>","Position comfortably with head slightly elevated and monitor ABCs<span class=\"zh\">舒适安置，头部略抬高，并监测 ABC</span>","Place in steep Trendelenburg position<span class=\"zh\">置于明显头低脚高位</span>","Give food and water<span class=\"zh\">给予食物和水</span>"],"answer":1,"why":"Correct. Keep the patient at rest, support the airway, and avoid oral intake while awaiting urgent transport.","zh":"正确。让患者休息、支持气道，并在等待紧急转运时避免口服摄入。","pearl":"In emergencies, recognize the pattern, stop care, position appropriately, support ABCs, give the indicated drug, and activate EMS without delay when needed.","rationales":[{"en":"Walking increases fall risk and may worsen neurologic injury.","zh":"行走会增加跌倒风险，并可能加重神经损伤。"},{"en":"Correct. Keep the patient at rest, support the airway, and avoid oral intake while awaiting urgent transport.","zh":"正确。让患者休息、支持气道，并在等待紧急转运时避免口服摄入。"},{"en":"Trendelenburg is not recommended and can worsen intracranial pressure.","zh":"不建议头低脚高位，且可能升高颅内压。"},{"en":"Food or water may be aspirated because swallowing can be impaired.","zh":"由于吞咽可能受损，食物或水可能导致误吸。"}]},{"id":"med-037","concept":"Respiratory","stem":"A patient is breathing rapidly, reports tingling around the mouth and fingers, and has clear breath sounds. What is the best initial approach?<span class=\"zh\">患者呼吸急促，口周和手指出现刺痛，但呼吸音清晰。最佳初始处理是什么？</span>","choices":["Assist with salbutamol immediately<span class=\"zh\">立即协助使用沙丁胺醇</span>","Coach slow controlled breathing and reassure the patient<span class=\"zh\">安抚患者并指导缓慢受控呼吸</span>","Place supine and give nitroglycerin<span class=\"zh\">仰卧并给予硝酸甘油</span>","Give epinephrine<span class=\"zh\">给予肾上腺素</span>"],"answer":1,"why":"Correct. The pattern is consistent with hyperventilation, which is managed with reassurance and controlled breathing.","zh":"正确。该表现符合过度换气，应通过安抚和控制呼吸处理。","pearl":"In emergencies, recognize the pattern, stop care, position appropriately, support ABCs, give the indicated drug, and activate EMS without delay when needed.","rationales":[{"en":"Salbutamol treats bronchospasm; clear breath sounds and tingling suggest hyperventilation instead.","zh":"沙丁胺醇治疗支气管痉挛；清晰呼吸音和刺痛更提示过度换气。"},{"en":"Correct. The pattern is consistent with hyperventilation, which is managed with reassurance and controlled breathing.","zh":"正确。该表现符合过度换气，应通过安抚和控制呼吸处理。"},{"en":"Nitroglycerin and supine positioning do not address this respiratory pattern.","zh":"硝酸甘油和仰卧位不能处理这种呼吸模式。"},{"en":"Epinephrine is reserved for anaphylaxis or other specific indications, not uncomplicated hyperventilation.","zh":"肾上腺素用于过敏性休克等特定情况，不用于单纯过度换气。"}]},{"id":"med-038","concept":"Respiratory","stem":"An asthma attack does not improve after the patient uses the rescue inhaler and breathing difficulty is worsening. What is the next priority?<span class=\"zh\">哮喘发作在使用急救吸入剂后未改善，呼吸困难正在加重。下一优先事项是什么？</span>","choices":["Continue dental treatment<span class=\"zh\">继续牙科治疗</span>","Call 911, provide oxygen if indicated, and prepare for deterioration<span class=\"zh\">拨打 911，按需供氧，并准备处理病情恶化</span>","Have the patient lie flat and wait<span class=\"zh\">让患者平躺等待</span>","Give oral glucose<span class=\"zh\">给予口服葡萄糖</span>"],"answer":1,"why":"Correct. Failure to respond to a rescue bronchodilator signals a severe attack requiring EMS.","zh":"正确。对急救支气管扩张剂无反应提示严重发作，需要 EMS。","pearl":"In emergencies, recognize the pattern, stop care, position appropriately, support ABCs, give the indicated drug, and activate EMS without delay when needed.","rationales":[{"en":"Continuing treatment increases stress and delays emergency care.","zh":"继续治疗会增加压力并延误急救。"},{"en":"Correct. Failure to respond to a rescue bronchodilator signals a severe attack requiring EMS.","zh":"正确。对急救支气管扩张剂无反应提示严重发作，需要 EMS。"},{"en":"Flat positioning can worsen respiratory distress and waiting is unsafe.","zh":"平躺可能加重呼吸窘迫，等待是不安全的。"},{"en":"Glucose does not reverse bronchospasm.","zh":"葡萄糖不能逆转支气管痉挛。"}]},{"id":"med-039","concept":"Allergy","stem":"A patient develops generalized hives and itching but has no airway swelling, wheezing, or hypotension. Which medication is most appropriate?<span class=\"zh\">患者出现全身荨麻疹和瘙痒，但无气道肿胀、喘鸣或低血压。哪种药物最合适？</span>","choices":["An antihistamine such as diphenhydramine<span class=\"zh\">抗组胺药，如苯海拉明</span>","Nitroglycerin<span class=\"zh\">硝酸甘油</span>","Insulin<span class=\"zh\">胰岛素</span>","Naloxone<span class=\"zh\">纳洛酮</span>"],"answer":0,"why":"Correct. A mild allergic reaction limited to skin symptoms is commonly treated with an antihistamine and close observation.","zh":"正确。仅限皮肤症状的轻度过敏反应通常使用抗组胺药并密切观察。","pearl":"In emergencies, recognize the pattern, stop care, position appropriately, support ABCs, give the indicated drug, and activate EMS without delay when needed.","rationales":[{"en":"Correct. A mild allergic reaction limited to skin symptoms is commonly treated with an antihistamine and close observation.","zh":"正确。仅限皮肤症状的轻度过敏反应通常使用抗组胺药并密切观察。"},{"en":"Nitroglycerin is for angina and can lower blood pressure.","zh":"硝酸甘油用于心绞痛，并会降低血压。"},{"en":"Insulin is unrelated and may provoke hypoglycemia.","zh":"胰岛素与此无关，并可能引起低血糖。"},{"en":"Naloxone is used for opioid overdose, not allergic urticaria.","zh":"纳洛酮用于阿片类药物过量，不用于过敏性荨麻疹。"}]},{"id":"med-040","concept":"Allergy","stem":"A patient develops throat tightness, wheezing, and hypotension minutes after a medication is given. What is the first-line drug?<span class=\"zh\">患者用药数分钟后出现喉咙紧缩、喘鸣和低血压。首选药物是什么？</span>","choices":["Diphenhydramine orally<span class=\"zh\">口服苯海拉明</span>","Intramuscular epinephrine<span class=\"zh\">肌内注射肾上腺素</span>","Nitroglycerin sublingually<span class=\"zh\">舌下硝酸甘油</span>","Glucose gel<span class=\"zh\">葡萄糖凝胶</span>"],"answer":1,"why":"Correct. Intramuscular epinephrine is the first-line treatment for anaphylaxis.","zh":"正确。肌内注射肾上腺素是过敏性休克的一线治疗。","pearl":"In emergencies, recognize the pattern, stop care, position appropriately, support ABCs, give the indicated drug, and activate EMS without delay when needed.","rationales":[{"en":"An antihistamine acts too slowly and does not reverse airway obstruction or shock.","zh":"抗组胺药起效过慢，不能逆转气道阻塞或休克。"},{"en":"Correct. Intramuscular epinephrine is the first-line treatment for anaphylaxis.","zh":"正确。肌内注射肾上腺素是过敏性休克的一线治疗。"},{"en":"Nitroglycerin may worsen hypotension and does not treat anaphylaxis.","zh":"硝酸甘油可能加重低血压，并不能治疗过敏性休克。"},{"en":"Glucose gel treats conscious hypoglycemia, not anaphylaxis.","zh":"葡萄糖凝胶用于清醒低血糖患者，不用于过敏性休克。"}]},{"id":"med-041","concept":"Allergy","stem":"An adult with anaphylaxis receives intramuscular epinephrine but severe symptoms persist. When may the dose generally be repeated according to the emergency protocol?<span class=\"zh\">成人过敏性休克患者已肌内注射肾上腺素，但严重症状持续。根据急救流程，通常何时可重复给药？</span>","choices":["Every 30 seconds<span class=\"zh\">每 30 秒</span>","Every 5 to 15 minutes as needed<span class=\"zh\">根据需要每 5 至 15 分钟</span>","Only after 2 hours<span class=\"zh\">仅在 2 小时后</span>","Never repeat it<span class=\"zh\">绝不重复</span>"],"answer":1,"why":"Correct. Epinephrine may be repeated at short intervals, commonly every 5 to 15 minutes, while EMS is activated and ABCs are supported.","zh":"正确。在启动 EMS 并支持 ABC 的同时，肾上腺素可按短间隔重复，通常每 5 至 15 分钟一次。","pearl":"In emergencies, recognize the pattern, stop care, position appropriately, support ABCs, give the indicated drug, and activate EMS without delay when needed.","rationales":[{"en":"Thirty-second repetition is too frequent and unsafe.","zh":"每 30 秒重复过于频繁且不安全。"},{"en":"Correct. Epinephrine may be repeated at short intervals, commonly every 5 to 15 minutes, while EMS is activated and ABCs are supported.","zh":"正确。在启动 EMS 并支持 ABC 的同时，肾上腺素可按短间隔重复，通常每 5 至 15 分钟一次。"},{"en":"Waiting two hours is dangerously delayed in ongoing anaphylaxis.","zh":"持续过敏性休克时等待 2 小时会造成危险延误。"},{"en":"Repeat dosing may be necessary when severe symptoms persist.","zh":"严重症状持续时可能需要重复给药。"}]},{"id":"med-042","concept":"Diabetes","stem":"A conscious patient with diabetes becomes shaky, sweaty, confused, and irritable. What should be given first?<span class=\"zh\">一名清醒的糖尿病患者出现颤抖、出汗、意识混乱和烦躁。首先应给予什么？</span>","choices":["A rapid oral carbohydrate source<span class=\"zh\">快速口服碳水化合物</span>","Insulin<span class=\"zh\">胰岛素</span>","Nothing by mouth and immediate discharge<span class=\"zh\">禁食并立即让其离开</span>","Nitroglycerin<span class=\"zh\">硝酸甘油</span>"],"answer":0,"why":"Correct. These are classic hypoglycemia signs in a conscious patient, so fast-acting oral glucose is appropriate.","zh":"正确。这些是清醒患者低血糖的典型表现，应给予快速起效的口服葡萄糖。","pearl":"In emergencies, recognize the pattern, stop care, position appropriately, support ABCs, give the indicated drug, and activate EMS without delay when needed.","rationales":[{"en":"Correct. These are classic hypoglycemia signs in a conscious patient, so fast-acting oral glucose is appropriate.","zh":"正确。这些是清醒患者低血糖的典型表现，应给予快速起效的口服葡萄糖。"},{"en":"Insulin would lower glucose further and may cause coma or death.","zh":"胰岛素会进一步降低血糖，可能导致昏迷或死亡。"},{"en":"The patient requires immediate treatment and monitoring, not discharge.","zh":"患者需要立即治疗和监测，而不是离开。"},{"en":"Nitroglycerin does not treat neuroglycopenia and may lower blood pressure.","zh":"硝酸甘油不能治疗神经低血糖，并可能降低血压。"}]},{"id":"med-043","concept":"Diabetes","stem":"A patient with suspected hypoglycemia is unconscious. Which action is safest?<span class=\"zh\">疑似低血糖患者已经无意识。哪项处理最安全？</span>","choices":["Place sugar under the tongue<span class=\"zh\">将糖放在舌下</span>","Give nothing by mouth, activate EMS, and administer glucagon if trained and available<span class=\"zh\">禁止口服，启动 EMS，并在受过训练且有药物时给予胰高血糖素</span>","Force the patient to drink juice<span class=\"zh\">强迫患者喝果汁</span>","Give insulin<span class=\"zh\">给予胰岛素</span>"],"answer":1,"why":"Correct. Oral substances can be aspirated; EMS and parenteral glucose-raising therapy are required.","zh":"正确。口服物质可能被误吸；需要 EMS 和非口服升糖治疗。","pearl":"In emergencies, recognize the pattern, stop care, position appropriately, support ABCs, give the indicated drug, and activate EMS without delay when needed.","rationales":[{"en":"Sugar under the tongue can still be aspirated in an unconscious patient.","zh":"无意识患者将糖放在舌下仍可能误吸。"},{"en":"Correct. Oral substances can be aspirated; EMS and parenteral glucose-raising therapy are required.","zh":"正确。口服物质可能被误吸；需要 EMS 和非口服升糖治疗。"},{"en":"Forcing fluids creates a major aspiration risk.","zh":"强迫饮用液体会造成严重误吸风险。"},{"en":"Insulin would worsen hypoglycemia.","zh":"胰岛素会加重低血糖。"}]},{"id":"med-044","concept":"Diabetes","stem":"Which presentation is more consistent with hyperglycemia than hypoglycemia?<span class=\"zh\">下列哪种表现更符合高血糖而非低血糖？</span>","choices":["Sudden sweating and tremor<span class=\"zh\">突然出汗和颤抖</span>","Rapid onset confusion after missing a meal<span class=\"zh\">漏餐后迅速出现意识混乱</span>","Gradual onset thirst, frequent urination, and dry warm skin<span class=\"zh\">逐渐出现口渴、尿频及皮肤干暖</span>","Immediate recovery after glucose<span class=\"zh\">给予葡萄糖后立即恢复</span>"],"answer":2,"why":"Correct. Hyperglycemia usually develops more gradually and is associated with thirst, polyuria, and dehydration.","zh":"正确。高血糖通常逐渐发展，并伴有口渴、多尿和脱水。","pearl":"In emergencies, recognize the pattern, stop care, position appropriately, support ABCs, give the indicated drug, and activate EMS without delay when needed.","rationales":[{"en":"Sweating and tremor are more typical of adrenergic hypoglycemia.","zh":"出汗和颤抖更典型于肾上腺素能性低血糖。"},{"en":"A rapid onset after a missed meal strongly suggests hypoglycemia.","zh":"漏餐后快速发作强烈提示低血糖。"},{"en":"Correct. Hyperglycemia usually develops more gradually and is associated with thirst, polyuria, and dehydration.","zh":"正确。高血糖通常逐渐发展，并伴有口渴、多尿和脱水。"},{"en":"Rapid response to glucose supports hypoglycemia, not hyperglycemia.","zh":"给予葡萄糖后快速恢复支持低血糖，而非高血糖。"}]},{"id":"med-045","concept":"Neurologic","stem":"A patient begins a generalized tonic-clonic seizure in the dental chair. What should the clinician do?<span class=\"zh\">患者在牙椅上发生全身强直-阵挛性癫痫发作。临床人员应怎么做？</span>","choices":["Restrain the limbs firmly<span class=\"zh\">牢牢约束四肢</span>","Place an instrument between the teeth<span class=\"zh\">在牙齿之间放置器械</span>","Clear the area, protect the head, lower the chair, and time the seizure<span class=\"zh\">清理周围、保护头部、降低牙椅并记录发作时间</span>","Give water immediately<span class=\"zh\">立即给水</span>"],"answer":2,"why":"Correct. Protect the patient from injury without restraining or placing objects in the mouth.","zh":"正确。应防止患者受伤，但不要约束，也不要将物体放入口中。","pearl":"In emergencies, recognize the pattern, stop care, position appropriately, support ABCs, give the indicated drug, and activate EMS without delay when needed.","rationales":[{"en":"Restraint can cause musculoskeletal injury and does not stop the seizure.","zh":"约束可能导致肌肉骨骼损伤，且不能终止发作。"},{"en":"Objects in the mouth can damage teeth and obstruct the airway.","zh":"口内放置物体可能损伤牙齿并阻塞气道。"},{"en":"Correct. Protect the patient from injury without restraining or placing objects in the mouth.","zh":"正确。应防止患者受伤，但不要约束，也不要将物体放入口中。"},{"en":"Giving water during a seizure creates an aspiration hazard.","zh":"发作期间给水会造成误吸风险。"}]},{"id":"med-046","concept":"Neurologic","stem":"When should EMS be activated for a seizure?<span class=\"zh\">癫痫发作时何时应启动 EMS？</span>","choices":["For every brief seizure in a patient with a known history<span class=\"zh\">任何已知癫痫史患者的短暂发作</span>","When the seizure lasts about 5 minutes, repeats without recovery, or is a first seizure<span class=\"zh\">发作持续约 5 分钟、反复发作且未恢复，或首次发作时</span>","Only if the patient bites the tongue<span class=\"zh\">仅在咬伤舌头时</span>","Only after the patient goes home<span class=\"zh\">仅在患者回家后</span>"],"answer":1,"why":"Correct. Prolonged, repeated, or first-time seizures require emergency medical evaluation.","zh":"正确。持续时间长、反复发作或首次发作需要紧急医疗评估。","pearl":"In emergencies, recognize the pattern, stop care, position appropriately, support ABCs, give the indicated drug, and activate EMS without delay when needed.","rationales":[{"en":"A brief typical seizure may be managed supportively if recovery is complete, although clinical judgment is required.","zh":"短暂且典型的发作在完全恢复时可支持性处理，但仍需临床判断。"},{"en":"Correct. Prolonged, repeated, or first-time seizures require emergency medical evaluation.","zh":"正确。持续时间长、反复发作或首次发作需要紧急医疗评估。"},{"en":"Tongue biting alone does not determine EMS need.","zh":"单纯咬舌并不能决定是否需要 EMS。"},{"en":"Delaying activation until after discharge is unsafe.","zh":"等到患者离开后才启动 EMS 是不安全的。"}]},{"id":"med-047","concept":"Toxicity","stem":"Immediately after local anesthetic with epinephrine, a patient reports palpitations, tremor, anxiety, and headache but remains conscious. Which reaction is most likely?<span class=\"zh\">含肾上腺素的局麻药注射后，患者立即出现心悸、颤抖、焦虑和头痛，但仍清醒。最可能是哪种反应？</span>","choices":["Epinephrine reaction<span class=\"zh\">肾上腺素反应</span>","Late-stage local anesthetic overdose with CNS depression<span class=\"zh\">局麻药过量晚期伴中枢抑制</span>","Hypoglycemic coma<span class=\"zh\">低血糖昏迷</span>","Anaphylaxis with airway obstruction<span class=\"zh\">伴气道阻塞的过敏性休克</span>"],"answer":0,"why":"Correct. Sudden palpitations, tremor, and anxiety immediately after injection are characteristic of an epinephrine reaction.","zh":"正确。注射后立即出现心悸、颤抖和焦虑，是肾上腺素反应的典型表现。","pearl":"In emergencies, recognize the pattern, stop care, position appropriately, support ABCs, give the indicated drug, and activate EMS without delay when needed.","rationales":[{"en":"Correct. Sudden palpitations, tremor, and anxiety immediately after injection are characteristic of an epinephrine reaction.","zh":"正确。注射后立即出现心悸、颤抖和焦虑，是肾上腺素反应的典型表现。"},{"en":"Late anesthetic toxicity is more associated with severe CNS and cardiovascular depression.","zh":"局麻药毒性晚期更常见严重中枢神经和心血管抑制。"},{"en":"The patient is conscious and the timing is linked to injection, not missed food.","zh":"患者仍清醒，且时间与注射相关，而非漏餐。"},{"en":"Anaphylaxis would more often include airway, skin, or circulatory findings.","zh":"过敏性休克更常见气道、皮肤或循环表现。"}]},{"id":"med-048","concept":"Toxicity","stem":"Which early sign is most suggestive of local anesthetic systemic toxicity?<span class=\"zh\">下列哪项早期表现最提示局麻药全身毒性？</span>","choices":["Circumoral numbness, tinnitus, metallic taste, or agitation<span class=\"zh\">口周麻木、耳鸣、金属味或躁动</span>","Localized gingival bleeding<span class=\"zh\">局部牙龈出血</span>","Gradual tooth sensitivity<span class=\"zh\">逐渐出现牙齿敏感</span>","Dry lips only<span class=\"zh\">仅嘴唇干燥</span>"],"answer":0,"why":"Correct. Early CNS excitation signs often precede seizures and later depression in local anesthetic toxicity.","zh":"正确。局麻药毒性早期常先出现中枢兴奋表现，随后可能发生癫痫和抑制。","pearl":"In emergencies, recognize the pattern, stop care, position appropriately, support ABCs, give the indicated drug, and activate EMS without delay when needed.","rationales":[{"en":"Correct. Early CNS excitation signs often precede seizures and later depression in local anesthetic toxicity.","zh":"正确。局麻药毒性早期常先出现中枢兴奋表现，随后可能发生癫痫和抑制。"},{"en":"Gingival bleeding is a local oral finding, not systemic anesthetic toxicity.","zh":"牙龈出血是局部口腔表现，不是局麻药全身毒性。"},{"en":"Tooth sensitivity is unrelated to acute systemic toxicity.","zh":"牙齿敏感与急性全身毒性无关。"},{"en":"Dry lips alone are nonspecific.","zh":"单纯嘴唇干燥缺乏特异性。"}]},{"id":"med-049","concept":"Toxicity","stem":"A patient develops signs of local anesthetic toxicity. What is the immediate priority?<span class=\"zh\">患者出现局麻药毒性表现。立即处理的首要事项是什么？</span>","choices":["Continue injecting slowly<span class=\"zh\">继续缓慢注射</span>","Stop administration, support airway and breathing, give oxygen, and activate EMS if significant<span class=\"zh\">停止给药，支持气道和呼吸，给予氧气，严重时启动 EMS</span>","Send the patient to the waiting room<span class=\"zh\">让患者去候诊室</span>","Give nitroglycerin<span class=\"zh\">给予硝酸甘油</span>"],"answer":1,"why":"Correct. Stop the source, maintain ABCs, provide oxygen, monitor, and escalate promptly.","zh":"正确。停止药物来源、维持 ABC、供氧、监测并及时升级处理。","pearl":"In emergencies, recognize the pattern, stop care, position appropriately, support ABCs, give the indicated drug, and activate EMS without delay when needed.","rationales":[{"en":"Continuing administration increases the toxic dose.","zh":"继续给药会增加毒性剂量。"},{"en":"Correct. Stop the source, maintain ABCs, provide oxygen, monitor, and escalate promptly.","zh":"正确。停止药物来源、维持 ABC、供氧、监测并及时升级处理。"},{"en":"The patient requires direct monitoring and emergency support, not isolation.","zh":"患者需要直接监测和急救支持，而不是被单独安置。"},{"en":"Nitroglycerin does not treat anesthetic toxicity and may worsen hypotension.","zh":"硝酸甘油不能治疗局麻药毒性，并可能加重低血压。"}]},{"id":"med-050","concept":"Dental complications","stem":"An instrument fragment or tooth is suspected to have been aspirated and the patient is coughing but still moving air. What should be done?<span class=\"zh\">怀疑患者吸入器械碎片或牙齿，患者正在咳嗽但仍有气流。应怎么做？</span>","choices":["Encourage effective coughing and monitor closely<span class=\"zh\">鼓励有效咳嗽并密切监测</span>","Perform blind finger sweeps<span class=\"zh\">进行盲目手指探查</span>","Give food to push it down<span class=\"zh\">给予食物将其推下</span>","Immediately lay the patient flat<span class=\"zh\">立即让患者平躺</span>"],"answer":0,"why":"Correct. With a partial airway obstruction and effective cough, encourage coughing while preparing to escalate if airflow worsens.","zh":"正确。部分气道阻塞且咳嗽有效时，应鼓励咳嗽，并准备在气流恶化时升级处理。","pearl":"In emergencies, recognize the pattern, stop care, position appropriately, support ABCs, give the indicated drug, and activate EMS without delay when needed.","rationales":[{"en":"Correct. With a partial airway obstruction and effective cough, encourage coughing while preparing to escalate if airflow worsens.","zh":"正确。部分气道阻塞且咳嗽有效时，应鼓励咳嗽，并准备在气流恶化时升级处理。"},{"en":"Blind sweeps can push the object deeper and injure tissues.","zh":"盲目探查可能将异物推得更深并损伤组织。"},{"en":"Food may worsen obstruction and is unsafe.","zh":"食物可能加重阻塞，不安全。"},{"en":"Flat positioning can impair breathing and does not remove the object.","zh":"平躺可能妨碍呼吸，也不能移除异物。"}]},{"id":"med-051","concept":"Dental complications","stem":"A conscious adult has a complete airway obstruction and cannot speak or cough. What is the appropriate response?<span class=\"zh\">一名清醒成人发生完全气道阻塞，不能说话或咳嗽。应采取什么措施？</span>","choices":["Give sips of water<span class=\"zh\">给少量水</span>","Begin abdominal thrusts and activate emergency response<span class=\"zh\">开始腹部冲击并启动急救反应</span>","Ask the patient to lie down and wait<span class=\"zh\">让患者躺下等待</span>","Perform chest compressions while standing<span class=\"zh\">站立时进行胸外按压</span>"],"answer":1,"why":"Correct. A conscious adult with severe complete obstruction requires immediate thrusts and emergency activation.","zh":"正确。清醒成人严重完全阻塞时需要立即进行冲击并启动急救。","pearl":"In emergencies, recognize the pattern, stop care, position appropriately, support ABCs, give the indicated drug, and activate EMS without delay when needed.","rationales":[{"en":"Water can be aspirated and does not relieve complete obstruction.","zh":"水可能被误吸，也不能解除完全阻塞。"},{"en":"Correct. A conscious adult with severe complete obstruction requires immediate thrusts and emergency activation.","zh":"正确。清醒成人严重完全阻塞时需要立即进行冲击并启动急救。"},{"en":"Waiting risks rapid hypoxia and cardiac arrest.","zh":"等待会造成快速缺氧和心搏骤停风险。"},{"en":"Standing chest compressions are not the standard first technique for a nonpregnant conscious adult.","zh":"对非孕清醒成人，站立胸外按压不是标准首选技术。"}]},{"id":"med-052","concept":"Dental complications","stem":"Persistent postoperative bleeding continues despite initial gauze pressure. What is the next best step?<span class=\"zh\">术后出血在初步纱布压迫后仍持续。下一步最佳处理是什么？</span>","choices":["Remove all pressure and observe<span class=\"zh\">停止所有压迫并观察</span>","Apply firm continuous pressure with fresh gauze and assess medical/medication history<span class=\"zh\">用新纱布持续有力压迫，并评估病史和用药史</span>","Rinse vigorously with hot water<span class=\"zh\">用热水剧烈漱口</span>","Send the patient home immediately<span class=\"zh\">立即让患者回家</span>"],"answer":1,"why":"Correct. Direct pressure is the first local measure, while anticoagulant use and systemic bleeding risk are assessed.","zh":"正确。直接压迫是首要局部措施，同时应评估抗凝药使用和全身出血风险。","pearl":"In emergencies, recognize the pattern, stop care, position appropriately, support ABCs, give the indicated drug, and activate EMS without delay when needed.","rationales":[{"en":"Removing pressure allows clot disruption and continued bleeding.","zh":"停止压迫会破坏血凝块并使出血持续。"},{"en":"Correct. Direct pressure is the first local measure, while anticoagulant use and systemic bleeding risk are assessed.","zh":"正确。直接压迫是首要局部措施，同时应评估抗凝药使用和全身出血风险。"},{"en":"Hot vigorous rinsing can dislodge the clot and worsen bleeding.","zh":"热水剧烈漱口会使血凝块脱落并加重出血。"},{"en":"Uncontrolled bleeding requires assessment and management before discharge.","zh":"未控制的出血必须在离开前进行评估和处理。"}]},{"id":"med-053","concept":"Priorities","stem":"Which item is essential in a dental-office emergency kit?<span class=\"zh\">下列哪项是牙科诊所急救箱中的必备物品？</span>","choices":["Epinephrine for anaphylaxis<span class=\"zh\">用于过敏性休克的肾上腺素</span>","A whitening agent<span class=\"zh\">美白剂</span>","Alginate impression material<span class=\"zh\">藻酸盐印模材料</span>","A temporary crown kit only<span class=\"zh\">仅临时冠套装</span>"],"answer":0,"why":"Correct. Epinephrine is a time-critical, life-saving emergency medication for anaphylaxis.","zh":"正确。肾上腺素是治疗过敏性休克的关键救命急救药物。","pearl":"In emergencies, recognize the pattern, stop care, position appropriately, support ABCs, give the indicated drug, and activate EMS without delay when needed.","rationales":[{"en":"Correct. Epinephrine is a time-critical, life-saving emergency medication for anaphylaxis.","zh":"正确。肾上腺素是治疗过敏性休克的关键救命急救药物。"},{"en":"Whitening material has no emergency role.","zh":"美白材料没有急救作用。"},{"en":"Impression material is not part of emergency pharmacologic support.","zh":"印模材料不属于急救药物支持。"},{"en":"A temporary crown kit is restorative equipment, not a life-saving emergency supply.","zh":"临时冠套装是修复设备，不是救命急救用品。"}]},{"id":"med-054","concept":"Priorities","stem":"During a serious emergency, which team action best improves efficiency and safety?<span class=\"zh\">严重急症发生时，哪种团队行动最能提高效率和安全性？</span>","choices":["Everyone performs the same task<span class=\"zh\">每个人都执行同一任务</span>","One person leads while others have predefined roles such as calling EMS, bringing the AED, and documenting<span class=\"zh\">一人负责指挥，其他人按预设角色呼叫 EMS、拿 AED 和记录</span>","Wait for the dentist before doing anything<span class=\"zh\">在牙医到来前什么都不做</span>","Move the patient repeatedly between rooms<span class=\"zh\">不断将患者在不同房间之间移动</span>"],"answer":1,"why":"Correct. Preassigned roles reduce duplication, omissions, and delay during high-stress events.","zh":"正确。预先分配角色可减少高压事件中的重复、遗漏和延误。","pearl":"In emergencies, recognize the pattern, stop care, position appropriately, support ABCs, give the indicated drug, and activate EMS without delay when needed.","rationales":[{"en":"Duplicating one task leaves other critical actions undone.","zh":"所有人执行同一任务会导致其他关键行动无人完成。"},{"en":"Correct. Preassigned roles reduce duplication, omissions, and delay during high-stress events.","zh":"正确。预先分配角色可减少高压事件中的重复、遗漏和延误。"},{"en":"Basic emergency response should begin immediately within each provider’s training.","zh":"应在各自受训范围内立即开始基本急救。"},{"en":"Unnecessary movement wastes time and may worsen the patient’s condition.","zh":"不必要的移动会浪费时间，并可能加重病情。"}]},{"id":"med-055","concept":"Documentation","stem":"Which medication detail must be included in the emergency record?<span class=\"zh\">急救记录中必须包含哪项药物信息？</span>","choices":["Only the colour of the package<span class=\"zh\">仅包装颜色</span>","Drug name, dose, route, time given, and patient response<span class=\"zh\">药名、剂量、给药途径、给药时间及患者反应</span>","Only who purchased it<span class=\"zh\">仅记录购买者</span>","No medication details are needed<span class=\"zh\">无需记录药物详情</span>"],"answer":1,"why":"Correct. Complete medication documentation supports continuity of care and legal accountability.","zh":"正确。完整的药物记录有助于连续照护和法律责任。","pearl":"In emergencies, recognize the pattern, stop care, position appropriately, support ABCs, give the indicated drug, and activate EMS without delay when needed.","rationales":[{"en":"Package colour does not communicate clinically useful information.","zh":"包装颜色不能提供有临床价值的信息。"},{"en":"Correct. Complete medication documentation supports continuity of care and legal accountability.","zh":"正确。完整的药物记录有助于连续照护和法律责任。"},{"en":"Purchasing information does not document patient treatment.","zh":"购买信息不能记录患者治疗。"},{"en":"Medication details are essential whenever a drug is administered.","zh":"任何给药都必须记录药物详情。"}]}];
